      "description": "Watch Pafos vs Red Bull Salzburg highlights and goals from UEFA Europa League on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on August 13, 2026. The UEFA Europa League served up an intriguing encounter on August 13, 2026, as Pafos hosted Red Bull Salzburg . Both sides took to the pitch under the floodlights, eager to claim vital points in this prestigious European competition. Salzburg Take Control Early The visitors from Austria established their rhythm early in the match, pressing high and forcing errors. In the 15th minute, the deadlock was broken when Lele found the back of the net, clinical in his finish after being set up by a clever assist from Bruno Felipe . While Pafos tried to find their footing, they struggled to contain the fluid movement of the Red Bull Salzburg attack. The pressure told again in the 37th minute when Biel scored a well-deserved second goal, ensuring the visitors went into the break with a commanding lead. The Haris Tabakovic Show The second half turned into a masterclass by Haris Tabakovic . The striker began his scoring spree in the 54th minute with a sharp finish. His momentum continued just four minutes later when Salzburg were awarded a penalty; Tabakovic stepped up and coolly converted from the spot in the 58th minute. Not content with a brace, he completed his hat-trick in the 70th minute, effectively ending any hopes of a comeback for the home side as the scoreline continued to widen. Late Impact and Full Time As the game entered its final stages, both managers utilized their benches. Murad Mammadov was introduced in the 82nd minute for Vlad Dragomir , and he made an instant impact. Just two minutes after his introduction, Mammadov found the target in the 84th minute to add a fifth for his side. Despite the late flurry of goals and tactical shifts, the intensity remained until the final whistle at 90+5 minutes, confirming a statement victory for the visiting team on Cypriot soil."
